      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Was suffering this issue bad today on a 9950X3D2 with Arch, native Steam, latest kernel & drivers, with any versions of Proton. Couldn't consistently change worlds, open menus, or stay in a world for too long before getting the SuspendThread crash.\n\nDisabling Esync and Fsync seemed to fix it for me. Set your VRC launch options to:\n\nPROTON_NO_ESYNC=1 PROTON_NO_FSYNC=1 %command%\n\nThis will likely cause a performance hit but I had no crashes in 3 hours after setting this when previously I would crash within minutes. Hoping it helps someone else. Also hoping we get whatever release this fix is coming to soon...",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
