      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5ba8889cfa86f032d1596de2|full_name} This inspired me to check if NTSync is enabled. NTSync is the newer in-kernel replacement for ESync/FSync. It wasn't enabled.\n\nTo check: `ls -l /dev/ntsync` (if this file exists it's enabled)\n\nTo enable it: `sudo modprobe ntsync`\n\nTo enable it on future reboots: `echo ntsync | sudo tee /etc/modules-load.d/ntsync.conf`\n\nWith this, I could play for over an hour without issues.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
